                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="also readily took the breast of his wife. When I asked for the reason of"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l30" HPOS="374" VPOS="2178" WIDTH="1769" HEIGHT="62" BASELINE="376 2219 2143 2222" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="376 2219 374 2230 387 2240 389 2240 391 2240 393 2240 2141 2234 2143 2222 2141 2191 2069 2180 2067 2180 2065 2180 2036 2189 2017 2180 2015 2180 2013 2180 2011 2180 1978 2189 1892 2180 1890 2180 1646 2189 1598 2180 1596 2180 1545 2189 1447 2180 1446 2180 1444 2180 1412 2189 1317 2180 1315 2180 1313 2180 1292 2189 1167 2178 1165 2178 376 2185 376 2219"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="the woman’s conduct, the Chukchee replied, “Who knows? Perhaps it is a"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l31" HPOS="376" VPOS="2244" WIDTH="1742" HEIGHT="51" BASELINE="376 2279 2118 2279" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="376 2279 376 2295 2118 2295 2118 2279 2118 2244 376 2244 376 2279"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="kind of incantation to insure the love of the young husband in the future.”⁴"/>
                    </TextLine>
<TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l32" HPOS="481" VPOS="2363" WIDTH="1664" HEIGHT="45" BASELINE="483 2388 2145 2394" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="483 2388 481 2402 2141 2408 2145 2394 2143 2365 483 2363 483 2388"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="¹ The practice of child-betrothal seems to be universal also among the American Eskimo, as mentioned"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l33" HPOS="378" VPOS="2408" WIDTH="1767" HEIGHT="42" BASELINE="378 2435 2145 2435" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="378 2435 378 2449 2143 2450 2145 2435 2135 2408 378 2408 378 2435"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="by Murdoch (Point Barrow Eskimo, p. 410). “Lucien M. Turner says, ‘Children are often mated at an early"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l34" HPOS="374" VPOS="2449" WIDTH="1769" HEIGHT="46" BASELINE="376 2480 2143 2474" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="376 2480 376 2493 2139 2495 2143 2474 2137 2449 374 2452 376 2480"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="age.’ I have known of several instances where two friends, desirous of cementing their ties of fellowship, have"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l35" HPOS="376" VPOS="2493" WIDTH="1767" HEIGHT="45" BASELINE="378 2521 2143 2517" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="378 2521 378 2538 2141 2538 2143 2517 2137 2493 376 2495 378 2521"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="engaged that their children, yet unborn, shall be mated.” Nelson mentions that very young boys are mated to"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l36" HPOS="376" VPOS="2532" WIDTH="553" HEIGHT="45" BASELINE="378 2560 929 2563" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="378 2560 376 2573 925 2577 929 2563 927 2536 378 2532 378 2560"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="quite small girls (Nelson, p. 291)."/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l37" HPOS="487" VPOS="2573" WIDTH="224" HEIGHT="53" BASELINE="489 2601 711 2604" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="489 2601 487 2612 600 2626 602 2626 709 2616 711 2604 709 2577 489 2573 489 2601"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="² See p. 372."/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l38" HPOS="485" VPOS="2614" WIDTH="1660" HEIGHT="51" BASELINE="487 2641 2145 2649" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="487 2641 485 2655 2141 2665 2145 2649 2143 2620 487 2614 487 2641"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="³ The same practice exists also among the American Eskimo. Murdoch (Point Barrow Eskimo, p. 411)"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l39" HPOS="376" VPOS="2659" WIDTH="1769" HEIGHT="51" BASELINE="378 2686 2145 2692" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="378 2686 376 2698 2141 2710 2145 2692 2135 2663 378 2659 378 2686"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="mentions, that, in one case he knew of, the bride was a girl of sixteen, and the husband a lad not over thirteen,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l40" HPOS="385" VPOS="2702" WIDTH="1618" HEIGHT="43" BASELINE="387 2727 2003 2731" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="387 2727 385 2741 1999 2745 2003 2731 2001 2706 387 2702 387 2727"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="who could barely have reached the age of puberty. The girl was living with another and older man."/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l41" HPOS="485" VPOS="2741" WIDTH="1662" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="487 2766 2147 2772" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="487 2766 485 2782 2143 2788 2147 2772 2145 2747 487 2741 487 2766"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="⁴ The marriage of full-grown girls to boys occurs among many other people more civilized than the"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l42" HPOS="378" VPOS="2786" WIDTH="1767" HEIGHT="44" BASELINE="379 2811 2145 2815" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="379 2811 378 2825 2141 2830 2145 2815 2137 2788 379 2786 379 2811"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="Chukchee. Among others, I will mention the Great-Russian peasants. Until recent times such marriages were"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l43" HPOS="376" VPOS="2827" WIDTH="1769" HEIGHT="44" BASELINE="378 2852 2145 2858" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="378 2852 376 2866 2141 2871 2145 2858 2135 2830 378 2827 378 2852"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="frequently contracted in Great-Russian villages; but, since the Great-Russians have no group-marriage, the rôle"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l44" HPOS="379" VPOS="2873" WIDTH="1766" HEIGHT="41" BASELINE="379 2899 2145 2899" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="379 2899 379 2914 2143 2914 2145 2899 2137 2873 379 2873 379 2899"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="of an actual husband would fall to the father-in-law. This is the so-called снохачество (from сноха, “daughter-"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l45" HPOS="378" VPOS="2910" WIDTH="1765" HEIGHT="49" BASELINE="379 2938 2143 2944" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="379 2938 378 2951 2139 2959 2143 2944 2141 2916 379 2910 379 2938"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="in-law”). Fathers-in-law acting as husbands are called снохачи. In a well-known old Russian anecdote, it is"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l46" HPOS="378" VPOS="2953" WIDTH="1767" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="379 2979 2145 2983" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="379 2979 378 2994 2141 3000 2145 2983 2135 2953 379 2953 379 2979"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="told that one time the people of a village ordered a new church bell. All the house-masters came and wanted"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l47" HPOS="379" VPOS="2996" WIDTH="1766" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="381 3023 2145 3027" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="381 3023 379 3035 2141 3043 2145 3027 2137 2998 381 2996 381 3023"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="to help hoist it to the belfry; but there was some hitch, and all efforts were without avail. Then the Pope"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-044_l48" HPOS="378" VPOS="3037" WIDTH="1765" HEIGHT="51" BASELINE="379 3062 2143 3070" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="379 3062 378 3078 2139 3088 2143 3070 2141 3045 379 3037 379 3062"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="bethought himself and exclaimed, “снохачи! hands off”, meaning that such hands were too sinful to take"/>
                    </TextLine>
</TextBlock></PrintSpace>
        </Page>
